  "title": "The Exact Resistance-Positivity Threshold for a Subdivided-Clique Join",
  "batch_label": "41",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every pair of integers m>=2 and ell>=1 with m<=2ell+3, the graph J_{m,ell}=K_ell vee H_m defined in source.md is resistance-positive. More precisely, J_{m,ell} has an explicit Hamiltonian cycle when m<=2ell+2; when m=2ell+3, the seven rational edge-orbit marginals stated in evidence/boundary_certificate.md lie in the relative interior of its spanning-tree polytope and have incident sum strictly below two at every vertex.",
